.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
docs/_build/
node_modules/

# Local workspace state
.worktrees/
.superpowers/

# IDE state. `.idea/` must be ignored in this file, not only via a developer's
# global excludesfile: the harness's hermetic `GIT_ENV` disables global git
# config, so deliver_candidate's dirty-repository preflight sees `.idea/` as
# untracked and refuses every /implement run.
.idea/

# Derived workload state: the bare clone cache and the cohort venv. Every
# committed manifest names its upstream and SHAs, so this is reconstructible
# and must never be committed.
.workloads/

# Mechanism-screen output. 570 files / 104.7 MiB were tracked here until
# 2026-08-12; they are archived out-of-tree, checksum-verified, and remain
# in this repository's history (`git log -- workloads/svcs/screen/`).
# `tools/screen_workload.py` writes new batches here by default, so without
# this entry the corpus would be re-committed a batch at a time. See
# docs/evidence-index.md for where the archive lives.
workloads/svcs/screen/

# Runtime state Pi writes into the harness-owned agent dir. Everything the
# harness *owns* there is listed explicitly above it in git; anything Pi
# creates at startup (an empty auth.json, sessions, caches) is not ours and
# must never be committed -- auth.json especially, since that is where a
# credential would land if a provider ever needed one.
pi-agent-dir/*
!pi-agent-dir/README.md
!pi-agent-dir/settings.json
!pi-agent-dir/models.json
!pi-agent-dir/extensions/
!pi-agent-dir/extensions/*.ts
